{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 131, :comments ["<b>My mouth</b> — For just as Your mouth opens to speak, my mouth I have opened, like one gasping to receive Your word." "<b>And the word יאבתי</b> — It has no cognate in Scripture."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 119, :notes {0 "The commentary appears to address a textual difficulty; the logic is compressed and the antecedent of 'Your mouth' is left unstated."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:40:49.694440690Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}